# L §2.4 "The loader accepts any spacing that the grammar allows" (tally 2.1.6, issue #81): a.fee (a.income[a.ana]),
# with a space before its (, is the member's band call a.fee(…), as f (x) is f(x), and prints touching: the same text
# and hash as L2_4_reprint_prefixed_call_member. tally 2.1.5's refcore took a prefixed call's ( only touching.
=== options reprint
=== J/joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "../A/ana.tally" sha256 "71199adf94c4e5b296f8a2a329994846c0bf935d86860bb2726beeecec6ea41e"

ask f: a.fee (a.income[a.ana]) law 2026-06-30
=== A/ana.tally
